<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Charles II of Spain</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1661">1661</a>–<a href="/years/1700">1700</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/17th-century">17th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Charles II of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/spain">Spain</a> was the last <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/habsburg-dynasty">Habsburg</a> king of Spain, reigning from 1665 to 1700. Sickly and childless, he presided over a period of economic weakness and military losses to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/france">France</a>. His will left the throne to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/philip-v-of-spain">Philip of Anjou</a>, grandson of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/louis-xiv">Louis XIV</a>, which brought the Bourbon dynasty to Spain and led to the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/war-of-the-spanish-succession">War of the Spanish Succession</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/charles-ii-of-spain.jpg" alt="Charles II of Spain" width="320" height="406" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Juan Carreño de Miranda · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Juan_de_Miranda_Carreno_002.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
